echo, fix: Gate B - refuse aliased roots, keep harvest spelling, trim descriptions

R13-01: both sync twins resolve canonical and both view roots through every
link in the path and its ancestors, and refuse (exit 2, no changes) when two
roots are the same tree or nested. Before this, a pool view linked to
canonical made the publish loop delete the canonical skill.
R13-02: git records harvest/ in lowercase; name reverted to harvest and the
local folder case fixed, so a fresh checkout matches.
Three descriptions trimmed under 650 chars (listing budget).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NJF6qVz7V5DeaWmDJ72aRK
echo, fix: Gate B - checker rejects unloadable YAML and reports config parity

B-01/R13-03: a plain scalar containing ': ' or ' #' is now a failure; a YAML
loader rejects or truncates it. Cross-checked against PyYAML on 48 files, 0
disagreements.
B-02: an owned skill set 'off' in Claude Code skillOverrides but published to
the Codex and Pi views is a failure. Today that is 7 skills; the enabled
roster is Eric's decision.
R13-02: directory spelling is compared with git's recorded spelling.

