Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NJF6qVz7V5DeaWmDJ72aRK
echo, fix: Gate B r2 - never read or write the manifest through a link

Both sync twins refuse (exit 2, no changes) when a view's manifest is a link
or not a regular file, before any mutation. The manifest is now written to a
new regular file and moved into place, so the old entry is replaced rather
than written through. Before this, a manifest linked to a canonical SKILL.md
was overwritten with the manifest text.

Verified: 13 scratch-HOME cases on bash 3.2 (incl. linked manifest, directory
manifest, second run leaves no temp files), PowerShell parse + the write path
on a real symlink, and a real sync (43 entries, drift 0).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NJF6qVz7V5DeaWmDJ72aRK
echo, fix: Gate B r2 - checker validates quoted/nested YAML and fails closed

K2-01: quoted scalars are checked for valid escapes and a closing quote on
the same line; nested and list-item lines are validated too; flow mappings,
anchors, aliases, tags, tab indentation and nested flow sequences are
rejected as unsupported. Fixed a bug where any empty-valued key (metadata:)
made every nested line skip validation.
K2-03: unreadable or malformed settings, a non-object skillOverrides, or a
failed git probe exit 2 instead of reading as 'no problems'.

Verified: 16/16 fixtures, 0 disagreements with PyYAML over the 42 real skills,
4/4 fail-closed cases, older fixtures unchanged. Real roster: 7 failing, all
the skillOverrides parity gap awaiting Eric's roster decision.

